.TH VORNISK 1 "July 2026" "vornisk 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vornisk \- fast, verified file copy and move
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vornisk
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fISOURCE\fR... \fIDESTINATION\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vornisk
copies or moves files and directory trees with per-file integrity verification
(xxHash3), an honest bandwidth throttle, dual progress bars, and atomic writes.
Every file is written to a sibling \fI*.part\fR temporary and renamed into place,
so a crash never leaves a half-written file at the final path. On a move, the
source is deleted only after the destination is written \fBand\fR verified, and
the emptied source directory tree is removed (directories still holding entries
are kept).
.PP
Symbolic links encountered while walking a tree are never followed; the summary
reports how many were skipped. Naming a symlink directly as a SOURCE argument
follows it deliberately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-move
Move instead of copy. Source files are deleted only after the verified write;
emptied source directories are then removed bottom-up.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Skip the verify pass (faster, less safe). Same-filesystem moves become an
instant rename.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Plan only: enumerate, count files/bytes, and detect destination conflicts
without touching anything. Combine with \fB\-v\fR to list every planned transfer.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIGLOB\fR
Exclude entries (repeatable). Patterns with \fB*\fR and \fB?\fR match the entry
name; a pattern containing a path separator matches the source-relative path.
Matching directories are pruned without walking their contents. Case-insensitive.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Concurrent file workers (default: min(4, CPU count)).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-limit " " \fIRATE\fR
Throttle, e.g. \fB512K\fR, \fB200M\fR, \fB1G\fR (base-1024 bytes/second).
Default: unlimited.
.TP
.B \-\-on\-conflict \fIMODE\fR
What to do when the destination file exists: \fBskip\fR (default),
\fBoverwrite\fR, or \fBrename\fR (numbered sibling).
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Shorthand for \fB\-\-on\-conflict overwrite\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-buffer \fISIZE\fR
I/O buffer size (default: 1M).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-preserve
Do not preserve timestamps and Unix permission bits.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
One line per file on stderr (ok/skip/FAIL, or the planned transfer under
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR). Disables the progress bars.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No progress, no summary.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable summary object on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-json\-progress
NDJSON progress events on stdout (one per ~200 ms tick), followed by the
summary object as the final line.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help (with the banner).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled (Ctrl-C).
.SH PAUSE AND RESUME
Standard job control works: \fBCtrl-Z\fR suspends the process,
.BR fg (1)
resumes it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Verified copy of a file into a directory:
.PP
.nf
    vornisk /data/backup.tar.zst /mnt/nas/backups/
.fi
.PP
Rehearse a large move first, excluding scratch data:
.PP
.nf
    vornisk -n -v -x '*.tmp' -x node_modules -m /srv/project /archive/
.fi
.PP
Throttled parallel copy to a NAS, scriptable result:
.PP
.nf
    vornisk -j 8 -l 300M --json --quiet /mnt/array /mnt/nas/backup | jq .success
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cp (1),
.BR mv (1),
.BR rsync (1)
